  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "high",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "The design features a critical attack path where untrusted input from a public GitHub issue can manipulate the agent into reading private repository data using a broadly scoped Personal Access Token, and exfiltrating it by creating a public pull request. The primary control is a human approval gate, but because arguments are collapsed by default and approval volume is high, it provides only partial mitigation (residual risk remains high). A model upgrade or further approval fatigue will bypass this gate entirely, triggering a critical forecast risk."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Assessment reflects declared design and configuration, not observed runtime behavior.",
